---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Legal &amp; ethics" description="The rights and ethics rules that govern Seichi Atlas.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p class="micro">Legal &amp; ethics</p>
      <h1 class="display-lg" style="margin:.7rem 0 1rem;">How this site stays honest</h1>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>
        Seichi Atlas is an independent fan-made reference. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
        or sponsored by any anime studio, publisher, or rights holder. All series titles are the
        property of their respective owners. The trademarks and series names appear here solely to
        identify the places associated with them.
      </p>

      <h2>What we don't publish</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Screenshots, clips, or artwork from any anime</li>
        <li>Character images or official logos</li>
        <li>Plot summaries or transcript-like scene descriptions</li>
        <li>Exact coordinates of private homes</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Respect for real places</h2>
      <p>
        Seichi is a real neighbourhood for the people who live there. Some sites have been closed
        after visitor misbehaviour. Our design choices reflect that: private residences are only
        mapped to the nearest station, schools appear as exterior-only notes, and etiquette guidance
        accompanies every site. <strong>Go quietly.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2>Takedown policy</h2>
      <p>
        If you hold rights over anything shown here, or you represent a location that prefers not to
        be listed, write to rights@seichiatlas.com. We will remove the content promptly and without
        argument.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; }
  .prose h2 { margin: 2.4rem 0 0.8rem; font-size: 1.35rem; }
  .prose p { margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; }
  .prose ul { margin: 0 0 1.4rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .prose li::marker { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
